<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="h-full w-full m-0 p-0 overflow-hidden">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    @* @Assets[...] gives each file a fingerprinted address (it changes when the file changes), so browsers may
       keep it for a year instead of asking again on every visit; MapStaticAssets serves it Brotli-compressed. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    @* Tailwind is compiled ahead of time (npm run build:css) instead of loaded from a CDN, so the page needs no
       third-party scripts and can run under a strict Content-Security-Policy. It comes after app.css, as the
       CDN version did, so its reset (e.g. links inherit their colour) still wins over app.css. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["css/tailwind.css"]" />
    <link rel="icon" href="favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="192x192" href="favicon.png" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="apple-touch-icon.png" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#003B5C" />
    <link rel="manifest" href="site.webmanifest" />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>

<body class="h-full w-full m-0 p-0 bg-gray-100 overflow-hidden text-gray-900 font-sans">
    <Routes />
    <ReconnectModal />
    <script src="@Assets["js/mermaid-render.js"]"></script>
    <script src="@Assets["js/review-output.js"]"></script>
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>